IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Parts V and VI (ss 60 to 65) and Schedule 1.
-- The definitions of ss 60, 64A(3) and 64B(1) are in vic-definitions.l4; the dates of s 64B(1) are in vic-interpretation-time.l4.
-- s 65 (regulations) is a regulation-making power and has no function here.

§ `Part V -- Authorised versions`

§§ `s 61 Effect of Part`

-- s 61: Part V is in addition to, and does not derogate from, section 54.
-- src:1220 | 61 Effect of Part
-- src:1221 | This Part is in addition to, and does not derogate from, section 54.
@ref s 61 (src:1220-1221)
GIVEN thePartTakesAwayFromSection54 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s61 Part V derogates from s 54` MEANS
    IF thePartTakesAwayFromSection54 THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 62 Authorisation of electronic version`

-- s 62(1): the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise an electronic version.
-- src:1225 | (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise an electronic version.
@ref s 62(1) (src:1225)
GIVEN isAnElectronicVersion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s62(1) the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the version` MEANS
    IF isAnElectronicVersion THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 62(2) and (3): an electronic version is an authorised electronic version if (a) it is in the format authorised by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel; (b) the words "Authorised Version" appear at its beginning;
-- (c) the words "Authorised by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel" appear at the foot of each page; and one that does not comply with subsection (2) is not an authorised electronic version.
-- Paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) are not joined by "and" or "or"; the function reads them as all required (the other reading is that any one suffices).
-- src:1226 | (2) An electronic version is an authorised electronic version if—
-- src:1227 | (a) it is in the format authorised by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel;
-- src:1228 | (b) the words "Authorised Version" appear at the beginning of the version;
-- src:1229 | (c) the words "Authorised by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel" appear at the foot of each page of the version.
-- src:1230 | (3) An electronic version which does not comply with subsection (2) is not an authorised electronic version.
@ref s 62(2) and s 62(3) (src:1226-1230)
GIVEN isAnElectronicVersion IS A BOOLEAN, inTheFormatAuthorisedByTheChiefParliamentaryCounsel IS A BOOLEAN, theWordsAuthorisedVersionAppearAtTheBeginning IS A BOOLEAN, theWordsAuthorisedByTheChiefParliamentaryCounselAppearAtTheFootOfEachPage IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s62(2),(3) the electronic version is an authorised electronic version` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT isAnElectronicVersion THEN NOTHING
        IF inTheFormatAuthorisedByTheChiefParliamentaryCounsel AND theWordsAuthorisedVersionAppearAtTheBeginning AND theWordsAuthorisedByTheChiefParliamentaryCounselAppearAtTheFootOfEachPage THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 63 Printed copy of authorised electronic version`

-- s 60 (definition of authorised version) and s 63: an authorised version is an authorised electronic version, or a printed copy of one in accordance with s 63;
-- a printed copy of an authorised electronic version is an authorised version only if it is printed directly from the authorised electronic version.
-- src:1204 | authorised version means—
-- src:1205 | (a) an authorised electronic version;
-- src:1206 | (b) a printed copy of an authorised electronic version in accordance with section 63;
-- src:1233 | 63 Printed copy of authorised electronic version
-- src:1234 | A printed copy of an authorised electronic version is an authorised version only if it is printed directly from the authorised electronic version.
@ref s 63 and s 60 "authorised version" (src:1204-1234)
GIVEN isAnAuthorisedElectronicVersion IS A BOOLEAN, isAPrintedCopyOfAnAuthorisedElectronicVersion IS A BOOLEAN, printedDirectlyFromTheAuthorisedElectronicVersion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s63 the document is an authorised version` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF isAnAuthorisedElectronicVersion THEN JUST TRUE
        IF isAPrintedCopyOfAnAuthorisedElectronicVersion THEN JUST printedDirectlyFromTheAuthorisedElectronicVersion
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 64 Evidentiary provisions`

-- s 64(1): an authorised version is on the mere production of that authorised version admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
-- src:1238 | (1) An authorised version is on the mere production of that authorised version admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
@ref s 64(1) (src:1238)
GIVEN isAnAuthorisedVersion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64(1) the document is admissible on its mere production` MEANS
    IF isAnAuthorisedVersion THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 64(2): it is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that a document purporting to be an authorised version is what it purports to be.
-- src:1239 | (2) It is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that a document purporting to be an authorised version is what it purports to be.
@ref s 64(2) (src:1239)
GIVEN purportsToBeAnAuthorisedVersion IS A BOOLEAN, theContraryIsProved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64(2) the document is presumed to be an authorised version` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT purportsToBeAnAuthorisedVersion THEN NOTHING
        IF theContraryIsProved THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Part VI -- General`

§§ `s 64A Appointment of non-citizens to public office`

-- s 64A(1) and (2): despite any rule of law to the contrary, the fact that a person is a non-citizen does not, of itself, affect the person's eligibility for appointment to a public office or disqualify the person from appointment.
-- Subsection (1) does not apply if the power to appoint is conferred by or under an Act or subordinate instrument and the contrary intention expressly appears in that Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:1249 | (1) Despite any rule of law to the contrary, the fact that a person is a non-citizen does not, of itself, affect the person's eligibility for appointment to a public office or disqualify the person from appointment to a public office.
-- src:1250 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if—
-- src:1251 | (a) the power to appoint a person is conferred by or under an Act or a subordinate instrument; and
-- src:1252 | (b) the contrary intention expressly appears in that Act or subordinate instrument.
@ref s 64A(1) and s 64A(2) (src:1249-1252)
GIVEN isANonCitizen IS A BOOLEAN, powerToAppointIsConferredByOrUnderAnActOrSubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppearsInThatActOrSubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64A the fact that the person is a non-citizen of itself affects eligibility for appointment to a public office or disqualifies the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT isANonCitizen THEN NOTHING
        IF powerToAppointIsConferredByOrUnderAnActOrSubordinateInstrument AND contraryIntentionExpresslyAppearsInThatActOrSubordinateInstrument THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 64B Validation--appointment of non-citizens to public office`

-- s 64B(1): purported appointment means a purported appointment of a non-citizen to a public office that was made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before section 64A came into operation.
-- The day s 64A came into operation is an input to the time module; the endnote day is in vic-interpretation-time.l4.
-- src:1258 | (1) In this section—
-- src:1259 | act or omission means an act or thing done or omitted to be done by an officer in the course of purportedly performing the functions and duties of a public office—
-- src:1260 | (a) whether before, on or after the commencement of section 64A; and
-- src:1261 | (b) whether or not under a power conferred by or under an Act or a subordinate instrument;
-- src:1262 | non-citizen has the same meaning as in section 64A;
-- src:1263 | officer means a person who was purportedly appointed to a public office by a purported appointment;
-- src:1264 | purported appointment means a purported appointment of a non-citizen to a public office that was made during the period beginning on 3 March 1986 and ending immediately before section 64A came into operation.
@ref s 64B(1) (src:1258-1264)
GIVEN isAPurportedAppointmentOfANonCitizenToAPublicOffice IS A BOOLEAN, dayTheAppointmentWasMade IS A DATE, dayS64ACameIntoOperation IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(1) the appointment is a purported appointment` MEANS
    IF isAPurportedAppointmentOfANonCitizenToAPublicOffice AND `s64B(1) the appointment was made during the period of a purported appointment` dayTheAppointmentWasMade dayS64ACameIntoOperation
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 64B(2): a purported appointment has, and is taken to always have had, the same force and effect as it would have had if s 64A had been in operation when it was made.
-- src:1265 | (2) A purported appointment has, and is taken to always have had, the same force and effect as it would have had if section 64A had been in operation when it was made.
@ref s 64B(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN isAPurportedAppointment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(2) the purported appointment has the force and effect it would have had if s 64A had been in operation when it was made` MEANS
    IF isAPurportedAppointment THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 64B(3): an act or omission is not ineffective, and is taken never to have been ineffective, only because of the fact that, but for subsection (2), the officer was not lawfully appointed.
-- src:1266 | (3) An act or omission is not invalid, and is taken to never have been invalid, only because of the fact that, but for subsection (2), the officer was not validly and lawfully appointed.
@ref s 64B(3) (src:1266)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatButForSubsection2TheOfficerWasNotLawfullyAppointed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(3) the act or omission is ineffective because the officer was not lawfully appointed` MEANS
    IF theOnlyGroundIsThatButForSubsection2TheOfficerWasNotLawfullyAppointed THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 64B(4): without limiting subsection (2) or (3), an act or thing done or omitted in reliance on the purported appointment, whether or not under a power conferred by or under an Act or subordinate instrument, and before, on or after the commencement of s 64A,
-- is not ineffective, and is taken never to have been ineffective, only because of the same fact.
-- src:1267 | (4) Without limiting subsection (2) or (3), an act or thing done or omitted to be done—
-- src:1268 | (a) in reliance, in whole or in part or directly or indirectly, on the purported appointment; and
-- src:1269 | (b) whether or not under a power conferred by or under an Act or a subordinate instrument; and
-- src:1270 | (c) before, on or after the commencement of section 64A—
-- src:1271 | is not invalid, and is taken to never have been invalid, only because of the fact that, but for subsection (2), the officer was not validly and lawfully appointed.
@ref s 64B(4) (src:1267-1271)
GIVEN doneInRelianceOnThePurportedAppointment IS A BOOLEAN, theOnlyGroundIsThatButForSubsection2TheOfficerWasNotLawfullyAppointed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(4) the act or thing done in reliance on the purported appointment is ineffective because the officer was not lawfully appointed` MEANS
    IF doneInRelianceOnThePurportedAppointment AND theOnlyGroundIsThatButForSubsection2TheOfficerWasNotLawfullyAppointed THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE VicActOrThingDoneInRelianceOnAPurportedAppointment IS ONE OF
    VicAJudgmentOrOrderOfACourtOrAnOrderOfATribunal    -- s 64B(5)(a)
    VicTheIssueOfAWarrantSummonsOrOtherProcess         -- s 64B(5)(b)
    VicAnyOtherActOrThing

-- s 64B(5): the acts and things referred to in subsection (4) include (but are not limited to) a judgment or order of a court or an order of a tribunal, and the issue of a warrant, summons or other process.
-- src:1272 | (5) The acts and things referred to in subsection (4) include (but are not limited to)—
-- src:1273 | (a) a judgment or order of a court or an order of a tribunal; and
-- src:1274 | (b) the issue of a warrant, summons or other process.
@ref s 64B(5) (src:1272-1274)
GIVEN actOrThing IS A VicActOrThingDoneInRelianceOnAPurportedAppointment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(5) the act or thing is one the acts and things referred to in subsection (4) include` MEANS
    CONSIDER actOrThing
    WHEN VicAnyOtherActOrThing THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE VicQuestionBeforeACourtOrTribunal IS ONE OF
    VicWhetherEvidenceObtainedAsAResultOfAnActOrOmissionOughtToBeAdmitted         -- s 64B(6)(a)
    VicWhetherARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityHasBeenAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred   -- s 64B(6)(b)
    VicAnyOtherQuestion

-- s 64B(6): for the purposes of a proceeding before a court or tribunal, the fact that, but for subsection (2), an officer was not lawfully appointed to the public office is to be disregarded in determining the question in (a) or (b).
-- src:1275 | (6) For the purposes of a proceeding before a court or tribunal, the fact that, but for subsection (2), an officer was not validly and lawfully appointed to the public office is to be disregarded in determining whether—
-- src:1276 | (a) evidence obtained (directly or indirectly) as a result of an act or omission, ought to be admitted; or
-- src:1277 | (b) a right, privilege, obligation or liability has been acquired, accrued or incurred.
@ref s 64B(6) (src:1275-1277)
GIVEN question IS A VicQuestionBeforeACourtOrTribunal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s64B(6) the fact that the officer was not lawfully appointed is to be disregarded in determining the question` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN VicAnyOtherQuestion THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Schedule 1 -- Style changes`

DECLARE VicStyleChangeRow HAS
    `column 1 old style`    IS A STRING
    `column 2 new style`    IS A STRING

-- src:1311 | | Sub-division | Subdivision |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 1 (src:1311)
`Sch 1 table row 1` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "Sub-division", "Subdivision"

-- src:1312 | | sub-section | subsection |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 2 (src:1312)
`Sch 1 table row 2` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-section", "subsection"

-- src:1313 | | sub-paragraph | subparagraph |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 3 (src:1313)
`Sch 1 table row 3` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-paragraph", "subparagraph"

-- src:1314 | | sub-sub-paragraph | sub-subparagraph |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 4 (src:1314)
`Sch 1 table row 4` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-sub-paragraph", "sub-subparagraph"

-- src:1315 | | sub-clause | subclause |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 5 (src:1315)
`Sch 1 table row 5` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-clause", "subclause"

-- src:1316 | | sub-sub-clause | sub-subclause |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 6 (src:1316)
`Sch 1 table row 6` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-sub-clause", "sub-subclause"

-- src:1317 | | sub-regulation | subregulation |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 7 (src:1317)
`Sch 1 table row 7` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-regulation", "subregulation"

-- src:1318 | | sub-rule | subrule |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 table row 8 (src:1318)
`Sch 1 table row 8` MEANS VicStyleChangeRow OF "sub-rule", "subrule"

`Sch 1 table` MEANS
    LIST `Sch 1 table row 1`, `Sch 1 table row 2`, `Sch 1 table row 3`, `Sch 1 table row 4`, `Sch 1 table row 5`, `Sch 1 table row 6`, `Sch 1 table row 7`, `Sch 1 table row 8`

-- Sch 1 cl 1: for an expression specified in column 1 of the Table, substitute the expression specified opposite it in column 2.
-- src:1308 | 1 For an expression specified in column 1 of the Table substitute the expression specified opposite it in column 2 of the Table—
-- src:1309 | Table
-- src:1310 | | column 1 old style | column 2 new style |
-- src:1311 | | Sub-division | Subdivision |
-- src:1312 | | sub-section | subsection |
-- src:1313 | | sub-paragraph | subparagraph |
-- src:1314 | | sub-sub-paragraph | sub-subparagraph |
-- src:1315 | | sub-clause | subclause |
-- src:1316 | | sub-sub-clause | sub-subclause |
-- src:1317 | | sub-regulation | subregulation |
-- src:1318 | | sub-rule | subrule |
@ref Sch 1 cl 1 (src:1308-1318)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Sch 1 cl 1 the expression substituted for the expression` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD row's `column 1 old style` EQUALS expression) `Sch 1 table`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (row's `column 2 new style`)

DECLARE VicSituationForAStyleChange IS ONE OF
    VicHeadingToAPartDivisionOrSubdivision                                  -- cl 2
    VicScheduleHeadingNumberAndTitle                                        -- cl 2A
    VicOtherScheduleHeadingOrPartHeadingWithinASchedule                     -- cl 2B
    VicFormHeadingNumberAndTitle                                            -- cl 2C
    VicNoteAtTheFootOfAProvisionNotUnderTheHeadingNoteOrNotes               -- cl 3
    VicNoteReformattedUnderClause3                                          -- cl 4
    VicDoubleQuotationMarksAroundADefinedWordOrExpression                   -- cl 5
    VicFullStopFollowingTheProvisionNumberAtTheBeginningOfAProvision        -- cl 6
    VicTitleOfAnActOrStatutoryRuleNotInItalicsWithoutBolding                -- cl 7
    VicLineAtTheEndOfAPartIndicatingTheEndOfThePart                         -- cl 8
    VicAnyOtherSituation

DECLARE VicStyleChange IS ONE OF
    VicSubstituteTheHeadingFormattedInTheSentenceCaseStyle
    VicSubstituteACombinedHeadingSeparatedByAnEmRuleInTheSentenceCaseStyle
    VicSubstituteTheNoteUnderTheHeadingNoteOrNotes
    VicOmitNoteColonAndMoveAnyNumberToTheBeginningOfTheNote
    VicOmitTheDoubleQuotationMarks
    VicOmitTheFullStop
    VicSubstituteTheTitleInItalicsWithoutBolding
    VicOmitTheLine

-- Sch 1 cl 2 to 8: the style change each clause makes; clauses 2, 2B, 2C, 3 and 7 apply only where the heading, note or title is not already formatted as the clause says.
-- src:1320 | 2 For a Part, Division or Subdivision heading that is not formatted using a style under which only the first letter of the initial word and of any proper noun is capitalised substitute that heading formatted using that style.
-- src:1322 | 2A In the case of a Schedule that has a heading designating the number of that Schedule and a title of that Schedule, for that heading and title substitute a heading combining that heading and title, separated by an em rule, and formatted using a style under which only the first letter of the initial word and of any proper noun is capitalised.
-- src:1324 | 2B For a Schedule heading (other than a Schedule heading to which clause 2A applies), or a Part heading within a Schedule, that is not formatted using a style under which only the first letter of the initial word and of any proper noun is capitalised substitute that heading formatted using that style.
-- src:1326 | 2C In the case of a Form that has a heading designating the number of that Form and a title of that Form, for that heading substitute a heading consisting of that heading and title, separated by an em rule, and formatted using a style under which only the first letter of the initial word and of any proper noun is capitalised.
-- src:1327 | 3 For a note at the foot of a provision that is not formatted under the heading "Note" or "Notes" substitute that note under the heading "Note" or "Notes" (according to whether there is more than one note at the foot of the provision).
-- src:1328 | 4 In a note that is reformatted in accordance with clause 3 omit the expression "Note:" and any number contained within that expression and insert that number (if any) at the beginning of the note.
-- src:1329 | 5 Omit any double quotation marks around a defined word or defined expression.
-- src:1330 | Note
-- src:1331 | Defined words and expressions are printed in bold italics.
-- src:1332 | 6 Omit the full stop immediately following the provision number at the beginning of a provision.
-- src:1334 | 7 For a title of an Act or a statutory rule that is not formatted in italics without bolding substitute that title formatted using that style.
-- src:1336 | 8 Omit the line appearing at the end of a Part indicating the end of the Part.
@ref Sch 1 cl 2 and Sch 1 cl 2A and Sch 1 cl 2B and Sch 1 cl 2C and Sch 1 cl 3 and Sch 1 cl 4 and Sch 1 cl 5 and Sch 1 cl 6 and Sch 1 cl 7 and Sch 1 cl 8 (src:1320-1336)
GIVEN situation IS A VicSituationForAStyleChange, alreadyInTheStyleTheClauseSays IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicStyleChange
`Sch 1 cl 2 to 8 the style change` MEANS
    CONSIDER situation
    WHEN VicAnyOtherSituation THEN NOTHING
    WHEN VicHeadingToAPartDivisionOrSubdivision THEN (IF alreadyInTheStyleTheClauseSays THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST VicSubstituteTheHeadingFormattedInTheSentenceCaseStyle)
    WHEN VicScheduleHeadingNumberAndTitle THEN JUST VicSubstituteACombinedHeadingSeparatedByAnEmRuleInTheSentenceCaseStyle
    WHEN VicOtherScheduleHeadingOrPartHeadingWithinASchedule THEN (IF alreadyInTheStyleTheClauseSays THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST VicSubstituteTheHeadingFormattedInTheSentenceCaseStyle)
    WHEN VicFormHeadingNumberAndTitle THEN JUST VicSubstituteACombinedHeadingSeparatedByAnEmRuleInTheSentenceCaseStyle
    WHEN VicNoteAtTheFootOfAProvisionNotUnderTheHeadingNoteOrNotes THEN (IF alreadyInTheStyleTheClauseSays THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST VicSubstituteTheNoteUnderTheHeadingNoteOrNotes)
    WHEN VicNoteReformattedUnderClause3 THEN JUST VicOmitNoteColonAndMoveAnyNumberToTheBeginningOfTheNote
    WHEN VicDoubleQuotationMarksAroundADefinedWordOrExpression THEN JUST VicOmitTheDoubleQuotationMarks
    WHEN VicFullStopFollowingTheProvisionNumberAtTheBeginningOfAProvision THEN JUST VicOmitTheFullStop
    WHEN VicTitleOfAnActOrStatutoryRuleNotInItalicsWithoutBolding THEN (IF alreadyInTheStyleTheClauseSays THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST VicSubstituteTheTitleInItalicsWithoutBolding)
    WHEN VicLineAtTheEndOfAPartIndicatingTheEndOfThePart THEN JUST VicOmitTheLine
